A||N||6||Springtyme||Windsheild wiper story =)||||10||
Z||000000||Springtyme||09-24-2001||12:52 PM||||Everytime I wash my car, my windsheild wipers go on and off by themselves for about the next 2 or 3 days. Well I washed my car on Saturday night and I unplugged them for the show yesterday. Well today I went to Walmart and it looked like it was gonna rain so while I was in the parking lot I plugged them back in. Needless to say, they still went on and off by themselves so I  pulled over on my way home to unplug them. As I was waiting for traffic to slow so that I could get out I saw a car pull up behind me. Well I got out and popped my hood and I was leaning over the side to plug them back in and the guy started talking to me...<P>What happened to your engine?<BR>Nothing, it's in the back<BR>You mean, in the trunk?<BR>You could say that<BR>Is it supposed to be there?<BR>Yes...<BR>Oh, okay. What are you doing?<BR>Unplugging my windshield wipers<BR>Why?<BR>So they dont go on and off by themselves<BR>Oh. So you don't need my help?<BR>No, but thank you anyway.<BR>Okay. *he walks away*<P>I waited until I got into my car and saw him drive away before I started laughing my @$$ off!!!!!!! That's the funniest thing that's happened to me yet. =)||||reg||10
Z||000001||Steve Normington||09-24-2001||06:37 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Springtyme:<BR><B>Is it supposed to be there?<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>ROTFLMAO!!!! <BR>||||reg||1
